      "content": "The strip reserved here by `navigationBarsPadding()` is left unpainted: the padding is applied to `SharedTransitionLayout`, so it shrinks the constraints of the `NavHost` below, and the only background in this subtree is `NavHost`'s own `Modifier.background(...)` (line 174), which therefore covers just the inset content area. Before this change `KomiScaffold`'s `Scaffold` filled the whole window with `colors.background`, so the area behind the (transparent, edge-to-edge) navigation bar matched the app theme; now the window background (`Theme.AppCompat.DayNight` → white/#303030) shows through, which does not match personalities such as AMOLED black or the manga paper tones.\n\nSuggestion: paint the container that also receives the insets, e.g. add `Modifier.background(LocalPersonality.current.colors.background)` at the start of this modifier chain (before `.padding(...)`, so the background also draws the padded area), or put the background on the outer `Box` at line 133.",
